    },
    {
      "block_id": "page-0486-block-0003",
      "order": 3,
      "text": "The intensity of the intolerance reaction is dose dependent, both with regard to the \namount of alcohol consumed and the dose of disulfiram. However, it is thought that \nmuch of the therapeutic effect is mediated by the mental anticipation of the aversive \nreaction, rather than the pharmacological action itself. Sudden death is more prevalent \nat doses above 1000mg.27 With this in mind, the value of prescribing higher doses of \ndisulfiram must be carefully considered.\n",
      "bbox": [
