    {
      "block_id": "page-0486-block-0005",
      "order": 5,
      "text": "The evidence for disulfiram is weaker than for acamprosate and naltrexone.2 In the \nUK, NICE recommends its use ‘as a second-line option for moderate-to-severe alcohol \ndependence for patients who are not suitable for acamprosate or naltrexone or have a \nspecified preference for disulfiram and who aim to stay abstinent from alcohol’.2\n",
